{"blocks":[["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-12","Banning AI from using specific words or phrases",["Ideas"]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-66","I'd like to make a system that makes it very easy for me to ban AI from using words and phrases with me or when creating documents.",["Ideas","Banning AI from using specific words or phrases"]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-202","My first thought about this was to make an AI/Agent/Skill in rulesync which would let me quickly add a word or phrase to a part of the knowledge garden that catalogs the words or phrases that I'd like AI to avoid when communicating with me or on my behalf, following progressive disclosure. I was thinking that ideally, there would be a table of contents page that would have logseq wikilinks to individual pages, one per word or phrase. That way listing the contents of a namespace would be sufficient to tell the AI what to ignore.",["Ideas","Banning AI from using specific words or phrases","I'd like to make a system that makes it very easy for me to ban AI from using words and phrases with me or when creating documents."]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-749","Later, I was thinking of using Claude/Code/Hooks for this.",["Ideas","Banning AI from using specific words or phrases","I'd like to make a system that makes it very easy for me to ban AI from using words and phrases with me or when creating documents."]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-817","Convert #tag links to [[wikilink]] form on commit",["Ideas"]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-877","I'd like a pre-commit converter, built like the text:fix-invisible mise task, that rewrites Logseq #tag and #[[Page]] links into [[...]] form — one obvious way to link (Py/Zen of Python), and the shape Looksyk can import, since it reads [[...]] but not #tag.",["Ideas","Convert #tag links to [[wikilink]] form on commit"]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-1162","Not as safe a rewrite as invisible whitespace, so it stays deferred. A # also begins headings, hex colors, shell comments, and URL fragments, so the converter has to skip fenced and inline code, ignore # before a space or another #, and treat # as a link only at a word boundary. Scope it to .md files under pages/ and journals/, where well over a thousand inline # links live today.",["Ideas","Convert #tag links to [[wikilink]] form on commit"]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-1576","fail2ban",[]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-1592","Person/James Clear",[]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-1618","Person/James Clear/Book/18/Atomic Habits",[]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-1666","Person/James Clear/Book/18/Atomic Habits/Quote/Good Easy, Bad Difficult",[]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-1745","My/Principle/Make the Right Thing Easy and the Wrong Thing Hard",[]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-1871","Py/Zen of Python",[]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-1895","My/Principle/Simplify/Not every distinction is worth recording",[]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-1965","Terminal/Multiplexer/Idea",[]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-1998","Logseq/Entity/Dotfiles/Dep/Idea",[]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-2037","Updated",[]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-2053","dependency intake vision",["Updated"]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-2081","My/Dotfiles/Process/Adding a New Global Dependency/Idea",["Updated","dependency intake vision"]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-2145","light formatting",["Updated"]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-2165","nvim",["Updated","light formatting"]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-2178","Lazygit",["Updated","light formatting"]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-2194","tmux",["Updated","light formatting"]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-2207","Yamtrack",["Updated","light formatting"]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-2224","mixed-metaphor example",["Updated"]],["2026-07-04%20Sat/","source-block-2250","My/Pref/Writing/Avoid Distractors such as Awkward or Superfluous Meta